    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (81.13) stands out as our clear offensive centerpiece. Despite facing Noah Schultz, whose elite skill set usually dampens expectations, the matchup efficiency is boosted by a favorable park factor and a premium batting order spot. **Bryce Harper** (68.35) follows closely as our second-strongest play; he is locked into the three-hole and possesses an impressive 0.388 xwOBA, though managers must monitor the 33% rain risk in his contest. Elsewhere, **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.09) and **Masyn Winn** (60.86) provide substantial value against favorable pitching matchups, with **Jung Hoo Lee** benefiting significantly from a dynamic platoon advantage that raises his efficiency floor.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving much of our secondary production, particularly for **Luis Arraez** (60.82) and **Jonathan Aranda** (49.59), whose situational splits against their respective right-handed opponents provide the necessary lift to keep them in starting roles. Conversely, **Cal Raleigh** (41.14) represents our most fragile start; he is facing a high-skill arm in Drew Rasmussen, and his production is further hampered by a negative park factor and an unfavorable platoon split. The most difficult bench decision involved **Dylan Beavers** (48.91), who narrowly missed the cutoff. While his leadoff projection and positional flexibility were attractive, his limited efficiency against the high-skill arm of Nathan Eovaldi and the need to preserve game caps ultimately pushed the optimizer toward more favorable matchups elsewhere. We remain cautious regarding **Justin Crawford**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Bryce Harper**, as potential weather delays in their respective venues could disrupt projected plate appearances.",
